{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3V8db5Joaun5NaMgK1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qw4fcxuaqUJi5GHbk4oeuD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat README.md config.py && echo ---- && cat -n server.py && echo ---- && cat logs/connect-attempt.log && echo ---- && cat logs/support-tickets.md","description":"Read README, config, server, and logs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":23302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":598},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1344e577-4446-40c6-a664-42bf20511b28","uuid":"6ac0089c-0e32-4d2c-8dc2-1899d5d3a989","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:37:20.762Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3V8Lj5PZ1fAcjbpTWp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Qw4fcxuaqUJi5GHbk4oeuD":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-Q8IX6v && cat README.md config.py && echo ---- && cat -n server.py && echo ---- && cat logs/connect-attempt.log && echo ---- && cat logs/support-tickets.md","description":"Read README, config, server, and logs"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Qw4fcxuaqUJi5GHbk4oeuD":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-Q8IX6v"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qw4fcxuaqUJi5GHbk4oeuD","type":"tool_result","content":"# tricoach\n\nBackend + single-page app for a small triathlon coaching practice. Coaches\nplan the week; athletes see it and connect their Intervals.icu account so the\napp can read wellness data and push planned workouts to their calendar. The\nathlete signs in to tricoach (token in `localStorage`, sent as\n`Authorization: Bearer` by the SPA's fetch wrapper), then clicks\n\"Connect Intervals.icu\", which runs the OAuth flow against Intervals.\n\n`server.py` is stdlib only (`python3 server.py`, port 8766) and keeps\neverything in memory; the shape is the same as the Postgres tables in prod.\nDev sign-in tokens: `tok-okafor` (default in the SPA) and `tok-rivera`.\n`config.py` holds the OAuth client placeholders. `logs/` has what we captured\nwhile looking into the connection problems.\nimport os\n\nPORT = 8766\nAPP_SECRET = \"dev-only-change-me-7c1f0a\"          # signs the OAuth state parameter\n\n# Intervals.icu OAuth client (placeholders; the real pair is in the deploy env)\nINTERVALS_BASE = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_BASE\", \"https://intervals.icu\")\nCLIENT_ID = \"tricoach-dev\"\nCLIENT_SECRET = \"s3cr3t-placeholder-0000\"\nREDIRECT_URI = f\"http://localhost:{PORT}/api/intervals/callback\"\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"\n\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\n----\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"tricoach backend: sign-in, Intervals.icu OAuth connection, wellness proxy.\n     3\t\n     4\tStdlib only. State is in memory (same shape as the prod tables).\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\timport base64, hashlib, hmac, json, os, threading, time\n     7\timport urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request\n     8\tfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n     9\t\n    10\timport config\n    11\t\n    12\tSTATIC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"static\")\n    13\tTOKEN_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/api/oauth/token\"\n    14\tAUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/oauth/authorize\"\n    15\tDEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n    16\t\n    17\t# --- in-memory store -------------------------------------------------------\n    18\tUSERS = {\n    19\t    \"tok-okafor\": {\"id\": \"u_okafor\", \"name\": \"C. Okafor\"},\n    20\t    \"tok-rivera\": {\"id\": \"u_rivera\", \"name\": \"T. Rivera\"},\n    21\t}\n    22\t# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\n    23\tCONNECTIONS = {}\n    24\tLOCK = threading.Lock()\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tdef log(msg):\n    28\t    print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[intervals]\", msg, flush=True)\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t# --- state parameter: carries the user through the redirect -----------------\n    32\tdef sign_state(user_id):\n    33\t    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"\n    34\t    sig = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    35\t    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(f\"{payload}:{sig}\".encode()).decode()\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef verify_state(state, max_age=900):\n    39\t    try:\n    40\t        user_id, ts, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")\n    41\t    except Exception:\n    42\t        return None\n    43\t    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\n    44\t    good = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    45\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(good, sig) or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:\n    46\t        return None\n    47\t    return user_id\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t# --- Intervals.icu calls ----------------------------------------------------\n    51\tdef post_form(url, fields):\n    52\t    data = urllib.parse.urlencode(fields).encode()\n    53\t    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"})\n    54\t    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n    55\t        return json.loads(r.read().decode())\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\tdef exchange_code(code):\n    59\t    return post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n    60\t        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n    61\t        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n    62\t    })\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef store_connection(user_id, tok):\n    66\t    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    67\t    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    68\t    if not refresh:\n    69\t        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n    70\t    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n    71\t    with LOCK:\n    72\t        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n    73\t            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n    74\t            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"refresh_token\": refresh,\n    75\t            \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\": \"connected\",\n    76\t        }\n    77\t    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\")\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef refresh_tokens():\n    81\t    \"\"\"Background pass: renew access tokens shortly before they expire.\"\"\"\n    82\t    while True:\n    83\t        time.sleep(config.REFRESH_INTERVAL)\n    84\t        now = time.time()\n    85\t        with LOCK:\n    86\t            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\n    87\t                if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:\n    88\t                    continue\n    89\t                if not c[\"refresh_token\"]:\n    90\t                    log(f\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\")\n    91\t                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n    92\t                    continue\n    93\t                try:\n    94\t                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n    95\t                        \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": c[\"refresh_token\"],\n    96\t                        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\n    97\t                    })\n    98\t                    c.update(access_token=tok[\"access_token\"],\n    99\t                             refresh_token=tok.get(\"refresh_token\", c[\"refresh_token\"]),\n   100\t                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))\n   101\t                    log(f\"{uid}: token refreshed\")\n   102\t                except Exception as e:\n   103\t                    log(f\"{uid}: refresh failed ({e}) -> expired, reconnect\")\n   104\t                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef intervals_get(conn, path):\n   108\t    req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{config.INTERVALS_BASE}/api/v1/athlete/{conn['athlete_id']}{path}\",\n   109\t                                 headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + conn[\"access_token\"]})\n   110\t    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n   111\t        return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode())\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t# --- HTTP ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n   115\tclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n   116\t    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):\n   117\t        print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[http]\", fmt % args, flush=True)\n   118\t\n   119\t    def send_json(self, code, obj):\n   120\t        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\n   121\t        self.send_response(code)\n   122\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n   123\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n   124\t        self.end_headers()\n   125\t        self.wfile.write(body)\n   126\t\n   127\t    def send_file(self, name, ctype):\n   128\t        p = os.path.join(STATIC, name)\n   129\t        if not os.path.isfile(p):\n   130\t            return self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n   131\t        with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n   132\t            body = f.read()\n   133\t        self.send_response(200)\n   134\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", ctype)\n   135\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n   136\t        self.end_headers()\n   137\t        self.wfile.write(body)\n   138\t\n   139\t    def redirect(self, url):\n   140\t        self.send_response(302)\n   141\t        self.send_header(\"Location\", url)\n   142\t        self.end_headers()\n   143\t\n   144\t    def current_user(self):\n   145\t        auth = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n   146\t        if not auth.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n   147\t            return None\n   148\t        return USERS.get(auth[7:].strip())\n   149\t\n   150\t    def require_user(self):\n   151\t        user = self.current_user()\n   152\t        if user is None:\n   153\t            self.log_message(\"%s %s 401 (no Authorization header)\", self.command, self.path)\n   154\t            self.send_json(401, {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n   155\t        return user\n   156\t\n   157\t    def do_GET(self):\n   158\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n   159\t        q = dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(url.query))\n   160\t        if url.path == \"/\":\n   161\t            return self.send_file(\"index.html\", \"text/html; charset=utf-8\")\n   162\t        if url.path.startswith(\"/static/\"):\n   163\t            return self.send_file(os.path.basename(url.path), \"application/javascript\" if url.path.endswith(\".js\") else \"text/plain\")\n   164\t        if url.path == \"/api/me\":\n   165\t            user = self.require_user()\n   166\t            return user and self.send_json(200, user)\n   167\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n   168\t            return self.auth_init()\n   169\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/callback\":\n   170\t            return self.callback(q)\n   171\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/status\":\n   172\t            return self.status()\n   173\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/wellness\":\n   174\t            return self.wellness()\n   175\t        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n   176\t\n   177\t    def do_POST(self):\n   178\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n   179\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":\n   180\t            user = self.require_user()\n   181\t            if user:\n   182\t                with LOCK:\n   183\t                    CONNECTIONS.pop(user[\"id\"], None)\n   184\t                self.send_json(200, {\"ok\": True})\n   185\t            return\n   186\t        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n   187\t\n   188\t    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\n   189\t    def auth_init(self):\n   190\t        user = self.require_user()\n   191\t        if not user:\n   192\t            return\n   193\t        params = {\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n   194\t                  \"scope\": config.SCOPES, \"state\": sign_state(user[\"id\"])}\n   195\t        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))\n   196\t\n   197\t    # Step 2: Intervals redirects back here with ?code=&state=.\n   198\t    def callback(self, q):\n   199\t        user_id = verify_state(q.get(\"state\", \"\"))\n   200\t        if not user_id or not q.get(\"code\"):\n   201\t            return self.send_json(400, {\"error\": \"bad state or code\"})\n   202\t        try:\n   203\t            tok = exchange_code(q[\"code\"])\n   204\t            store_connection(user_id, tok)\n   205\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n   206\t            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: HTTP {e.code} {e.read()[:200]!r}\")\n   207\t            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n   208\t        except Exception as e:\n   209\t            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: {e}\")\n   210\t            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n   211\t        self.redirect(\"/?connected=1\")\n   212\t\n   213\t    def status(self):\n   214\t        user = self.require_user()\n   215\t        if not user:\n   216\t            return\n   217\t        with LOCK:\n   218\t            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n   219\t        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n   220\t            return self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": False, \"status\": c[\"status\"] if c else \"disconnected\"})\n   221\t        self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": True, \"status\": \"connected\", \"scope\": c[\"scope\"],\n   222\t                             \"athlete\": {\"id\": c[\"athlete_id\"], \"name\": c[\"athlete_name\"]}})\n   223\t\n   224\t    def wellness(self):\n   225\t        user = self.require_user()\n   226\t        if not user:\n   227\t            return\n   228\t        with LOCK:\n   229\t            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n   230\t        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n   231\t            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n   232\t        try:\n   233\t            code, data = intervals_get(c, \"/wellness\")\n   234\t            self.send_json(code, data)\n   235\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n   236\t            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})\n   237\t        except Exception as e:\n   238\t            self.send_json(502, {\"error\": str(e)})\n   239\t\n   240\t\n   241\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   242\t    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\n   243\t    log(f\"serving on http://localhost:{config.PORT} (intervals: {config.INTERVALS_BASE})\")\n   244\t    ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", config.PORT), Handler).serve_forever()\n----\n### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n----\n# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1344e577-4446-40c6-a664-42bf20511b28","uuid":"9cb7c11b-f60d-4267-88e2-cfa695965122","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:37:20.799Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# tricoach\n\nBackend + single-page app for a small triathlon coaching practice. Coaches\nplan the week; athletes see it and connect their Intervals.icu account so the\napp can read wellness data and push planned workouts to their calendar. The\nathlete signs in to tricoach (token in `localStorage`, sent as\n`Authorization: Bearer` by the SPA's fetch wrapper), then clicks\n\"Connect Intervals.icu\", which runs the OAuth flow against Intervals.\n\n`server.py` is stdlib only (`python3 server.py`, port 8766) and keeps\neverything in memory; the shape is the same as the Postgres tables in prod.\nDev sign-in tokens: `tok-okafor` (default in the SPA) and `tok-rivera`.\n`config.py` holds the OAuth client placeholders. `logs/` has what we captured\nwhile looking into the connection problems.\nimport os\n\nPORT = 8766\nAPP_SECRET = \"dev-only-change-me-7c1f0a\"          # signs the OAuth state parameter\n\n# Intervals.icu OAuth client (placeholders; the real pair is in the deploy env)\nINTERVALS_BASE = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_BASE\", \"https://intervals.icu\")\nCLIENT_ID = \"tricoach-dev\"\nCLIENT_SECRET = \"s3cr3t-placeholder-0000\"\nREDIRECT_URI = f\"http://localhost:{PORT}/api/intervals/callback\"\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"\n\nREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher\n----\n     1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n     2\t\"\"\"tricoach backend: sign-in, Intervals.icu OAuth connection, wellness proxy.\n     3\t\n     4\tStdlib only. State is in memory (same shape as the prod tables).\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\timport base64, hashlib, hmac, json, os, threading, time\n     7\timport urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request\n     8\tfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n     9\t\n    10\timport config\n    11\t\n    12\tSTATIC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"static\")\n    13\tTOKEN_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/api/oauth/token\"\n    14\tAUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/oauth/authorize\"\n    15\tDEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n    16\t\n    17\t# --- in-memory store -------------------------------------------------------\n    18\tUSERS = {\n    19\t    \"tok-okafor\": {\"id\": \"u_okafor\", \"name\": \"C. Okafor\"},\n    20\t    \"tok-rivera\": {\"id\": \"u_rivera\", \"name\": \"T. Rivera\"},\n    21\t}\n    22\t# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\n    23\tCONNECTIONS = {}\n    24\tLOCK = threading.Lock()\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\tdef log(msg):\n    28\t    print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[intervals]\", msg, flush=True)\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t# --- state parameter: carries the user through the redirect -----------------\n    32\tdef sign_state(user_id):\n    33\t    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"\n    34\t    sig = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    35\t    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(f\"{payload}:{sig}\".encode()).decode()\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef verify_state(state, max_age=900):\n    39\t    try:\n    40\t        user_id, ts, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")\n    41\t    except Exception:\n    42\t        return None\n    43\t    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\n    44\t    good = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n    45\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(good, sig) or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:\n    46\t        return None\n    47\t    return user_id\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t# --- Intervals.icu calls ----------------------------------------------------\n    51\tdef post_form(url, fields):\n    52\t    data = urllib.parse.urlencode(fields).encode()\n    53\t    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"})\n    54\t    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n    55\t        return json.loads(r.read().decode())\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\tdef exchange_code(code):\n    59\t    return post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n    60\t        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n    61\t        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n    62\t    })\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef store_connection(user_id, tok):\n    66\t    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    67\t    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    68\t    if not refresh:\n    69\t        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n    70\t    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n    71\t    with LOCK:\n    72\t        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n    73\t            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n    74\t            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"refresh_token\": refresh,\n    75\t            \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\": \"connected\",\n    76\t        }\n    77\t    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\")\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef refresh_tokens():\n    81\t    \"\"\"Background pass: renew access tokens shortly before they expire.\"\"\"\n    82\t    while True:\n    83\t        time.sleep(config.REFRESH_INTERVAL)\n    84\t        now = time.time()\n    85\t        with LOCK:\n    86\t            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\n    87\t                if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:\n    88\t                    continue\n    89\t                if not c[\"refresh_token\"]:\n    90\t                    log(f\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\")\n    91\t                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n    92\t                    continue\n    93\t                try:\n    94\t                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n    95\t                        \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": c[\"refresh_token\"],\n    96\t                        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\n    97\t                    })\n    98\t                    c.update(access_token=tok[\"access_token\"],\n    99\t                             refresh_token=tok.get(\"refresh_token\", c[\"refresh_token\"]),\n   100\t                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))\n   101\t                    log(f\"{uid}: token refreshed\")\n   102\t                except Exception as e:\n   103\t                    log(f\"{uid}: refresh failed ({e}) -> expired, reconnect\")\n   104\t                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef intervals_get(conn, path):\n   108\t    req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{config.INTERVALS_BASE}/api/v1/athlete/{conn['athlete_id']}{path}\",\n   109\t                                 headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + conn[\"access_token\"]})\n   110\t    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n   111\t        return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode())\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t# --- HTTP ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n   115\tclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n   116\t    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):\n   117\t        print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[http]\", fmt % args, flush=True)\n   118\t\n   119\t    def send_json(self, code, obj):\n   120\t        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\n   121\t        self.send_response(code)\n   122\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n   123\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n   124\t        self.end_headers()\n   125\t        self.wfile.write(body)\n   126\t\n   127\t    def send_file(self, name, ctype):\n   128\t        p = os.path.join(STATIC, name)\n   129\t        if not os.path.isfile(p):\n   130\t            return self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n   131\t        with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n   132\t            body = f.read()\n   133\t        self.send_response(200)\n   134\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", ctype)\n   135\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n   136\t        self.end_headers()\n   137\t        self.wfile.write(body)\n   138\t\n   139\t    def redirect(self, url):\n   140\t        self.send_response(302)\n   141\t        self.send_header(\"Location\", url)\n   142\t        self.end_headers()\n   143\t\n   144\t    def current_user(self):\n   145\t        auth = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n   146\t        if not auth.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n   147\t            return None\n   148\t        return USERS.get(auth[7:].strip())\n   149\t\n   150\t    def require_user(self):\n   151\t        user = self.current_user()\n   152\t        if user is None:\n   153\t            self.log_message(\"%s %s 401 (no Authorization header)\", self.command, self.path)\n   154\t            self.send_json(401, {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n   155\t        return user\n   156\t\n   157\t    def do_GET(self):\n   158\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n   159\t        q = dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(url.query))\n   160\t        if url.path == \"/\":\n   161\t            return self.send_file(\"index.html\", \"text/html; charset=utf-8\")\n   162\t        if url.path.startswith(\"/static/\"):\n   163\t            return self.send_file(os.path.basename(url.path), \"application/javascript\" if url.path.endswith(\".js\") else \"text/plain\")\n   164\t        if url.path == \"/api/me\":\n   165\t            user = self.require_user()\n   166\t            return user and self.send_json(200, user)\n   167\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n   168\t            return self.auth_init()\n   169\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/callback\":\n   170\t            return self.callback(q)\n   171\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/status\":\n   172\t            return self.status()\n   173\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/wellness\":\n   174\t            return self.wellness()\n   175\t        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n   176\t\n   177\t    def do_POST(self):\n   178\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n   179\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":\n   180\t            user = self.require_user()\n   181\t            if user:\n   182\t                with LOCK:\n   183\t                    CONNECTIONS.pop(user[\"id\"], None)\n   184\t                self.send_json(200, {\"ok\": True})\n   185\t            return\n   186\t        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n   187\t\n   188\t    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\n   189\t    def auth_init(self):\n   190\t        user = self.require_user()\n   191\t        if not user:\n   192\t            return\n   193\t        params = {\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n   194\t                  \"scope\": config.SCOPES, \"state\": sign_state(user[\"id\"])}\n   195\t        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))\n   196\t\n   197\t    # Step 2: Intervals redirects back here with ?code=&state=.\n   198\t    def callback(self, q):\n   199\t        user_id = verify_state(q.get(\"state\", \"\"))\n   200\t        if not user_id or not q.get(\"code\"):\n   201\t            return self.send_json(400, {\"error\": \"bad state or code\"})\n   202\t        try:\n   203\t            tok = exchange_code(q[\"code\"])\n   204\t            store_connection(user_id, tok)\n   205\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n   206\t            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: HTTP {e.code} {e.read()[:200]!r}\")\n   207\t            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n   208\t        except Exception as e:\n   209\t            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: {e}\")\n   210\t            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n   211\t        self.redirect(\"/?connected=1\")\n   212\t\n   213\t    def status(self):\n   214\t        user = self.require_user()\n   215\t        if not user:\n   216\t            return\n   217\t        with LOCK:\n   218\t            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n   219\t        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n   220\t            return self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": False, \"status\": c[\"status\"] if c else \"disconnected\"})\n   221\t        self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": True, \"status\": \"connected\", \"scope\": c[\"scope\"],\n   222\t                             \"athlete\": {\"id\": c[\"athlete_id\"], \"name\": c[\"athlete_name\"]}})\n   223\t\n   224\t    def wellness(self):\n   225\t        user = self.require_user()\n   226\t        if not user:\n   227\t            return\n   228\t        with LOCK:\n   229\t            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n   230\t        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n   231\t            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n   232\t        try:\n   233\t            code, data = intervals_get(c, \"/wellness\")\n   234\t            self.send_json(code, data)\n   235\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n   236\t            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})\n   237\t        except Exception as e:\n   238\t            self.send_json(502, {\"error\": str(e)})\n   239\t\n   240\t\n   241\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   242\t    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\n   243\t    log(f\"serving on http://localhost:{config.PORT} (intervals: {config.INTERVALS_BASE})\")\n   244\t    ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", config.PORT), Handler).serve_forever()\n----\n### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n\n    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n    Request Method:  GET\n    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n\n### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n\n$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\nHTTP/2 400\ncontent-type: application/json\ncache-control: no-store\n\n{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n\n    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n\n### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n\n2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n----\n# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qw4fcxuaqUJi5GHbk4oeuD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
